# Nothing in this repository is Prettier's to reformat.
#
# Ocean is zero-dependency by design: every YAML file here is read by a hand-written
# parser in the former shell CLI (since removed), or by line-oriented shell
# (grep '^key:' and a tab-indentation check).
# Those parsers are deliberately strict — they reject what they do not understand rather
# than guessing — so a purely cosmetic reflow is a breaking change.
#
# This is not hypothetical. A format-on-save pass moved flow maps onto the line after
# their key:
#
#     skills:
#       { path: ~/.codex/skills/, format: SKILL.md+frontmatter, verified: true }
#
# Both manifests became unreadable, and every tool that resolves clients from the
# registry failed with them: tests/test-contract.sh went from 3 failures to 13.
#
# The parser has since been taught to read the wrapped form too, so a formatter is no
# longer able to break the registry on its own. This file is the belt to that braces:
# don't reflow files whose readers are stricter than YAML.

# Adapter manifests — read by the strict subset parser.
adapters/

# Capability manifests — read by the same parser.
capabilities/
# Compatibility window: the pre-rename directory name, still ignored if one exists.
plugins/

# Domain manifests — read by the same parser.
domains/

# Governance policies — read by the same parser and by line-oriented shell.
governance/
# Compatibility window: the pre-move policy root, still ignored if one exists.
policies/

# Templates seeded into the private workspace; settings.yaml is grepped, not parsed.
templates/

# Shell and Python tools, and the fixtures the contract suite compares byte for byte.
cli/
tests/

# Markdown carrying ```yaml fences that document the exact on-disk layout. Prettier
# reformats inside fenced code blocks, so the documented form drifts from the real one.
contracts/
docs/
skills/
README.md
AGENTS.md
